Windows/iOS: trap and untrap self-modifying-code pages per 16 KB host page

The iOS host page is 16 KB and Wine gives it the union of its four 4 KB
pages' protections. FEX armed its write trap (PAGE_EXECUTE_READ) on single
4 KB pages, so a host page with one trapped and one writable (or hot) 4 KB
page stayed writable: writes to the trapped page never faulted and FEX kept
running stale translations.

- The Escapists 2 (32-bit Unity, MADEIRA_WOW_RWX_PLAIN=1): Mono rewrote one
  call site ~40,000 times a second (WOW64 module).
- Project Zomboid (Zulu 25, code cache as plain memory, [x64-rwx]): the JVM
  spun in Runtime1::patch_code at 100% (ARM64EC module).

With FEX_IOS_HOST, traps are armed and released per host page, a write fault
invalidates and untraps the whole host page (each RWX 4 KB page with its own
untrap protection), and hot SMC pages are tracked per host page. Both
modules.

Applies on willfaust/FEX 6fb1b50 (Madeira's FEX pin). The shipped
app/Madeira/aarch64-windows/xtajit.dll and arm64ec-windows/xtajit64.dll are
built from 6fb1b50 + this patch with build/fex-wow64/build.sh and
build/fex-arm64ec/build.sh (llvm-mingw 20260421). Madeira-only: not for
FEX-Emu.

